expression: s
---
Decode base64 input (standard alphabet, with padding).

Examples: ubertool base64 decode aGVsbG8= ubertool base64 decode aGVsbG8= --json

Exit codes specific to this command: 3   invalid base64 (input could not be decoded)

Usage: ubertool base64 decode [OPTIONS] [INPUT]

Arguments:
  [INPUT]
          Literal base64 input to decode (omit to read from --in or stdin)

Options:
      --in <IN_PATH>
          Read base64 input from file

      --json
          Output as JSON to stdout. Human messages still go to stderr

      --out <OUT_PATH>
          Write decoded bytes to file. If absent and bytes are valid UTF-8, emits as text; otherwise refuses to write binary to a TTY

  -q, --quiet
          Bare values only (pipe-friendly)

  -v, --verbose
          Verbose progress to stderr

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

  -V, --version
          Print version
